note S5 scrub emit with floats: the output sha256 (s5.cases s5-scrub-femit) pins which V registers scrub
note zeroes when floats are live. f has the f64 parameter a (its value in x register X0, so its twin V16
note is dead), the parameter n (X1, twin V17 dead) and the f64 local x, which lives in the twin V18 of its
note slot. scrub zeroes V0-V17 and V19-V31 and spares V18 only: a twin is spared exactly when its slot is
note live and holds its value there. Sparing every twin of a live slot (V16, V17 too) or none (V18 too,
note omc 24caacf4) changes the output (s5-mutants.cases m-twinall, m-twinnone).
om2
fn f a f64 n ulong to f64
x = add a f64 1.0
k = scrub n
ret add x f64 k
end
fn main to int
r = f f64 2.0 32
if ne r f64 3.0
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
